<p>A carousel is a story in slides. Three things make it feel like one piece rather than five posts:</p>
<ul>
	<li><b>The thread.</b> A red line (<code>im-poster-thread</code>) runs across every slide at the same height, starting halfway through the first and ending halfway through the last. A swipe feels like turning a page of one thing.</li>
	<li><b>The counter.</b> <code>01/05</code> in pixel type, top left, every slide. People finish what they can see the end of.</li>
	<li><b>One idea per slide.</b> A slide that needs a scroll inside it is two slides.</li>
</ul>
<p>The first slide is a thumbnail: it has to earn the swipe alone. The last slide asks for one thing — save, share, or follow — never all three.</p>

